# Netlify SPA fallback — needed as of 2026-08-31, now that main.dart calls
# usePathUrlStrategy() (see its own comment for why: fixing the password-
# reset link, which needs a real path like /reset-password rather than
# Flutter web's default /#/reset-password).
#
# Under the OLD hash-based routing this file was never necessary — every
# route lived after a # fragment, which browsers never send to the server,
# so Netlify only ever needed to serve / (index.html) and the app's own
# router handled everything past the #. Under path-based routing, a direct
# load of any other route — clicking the password-reset email link and
# landing straight on /reset-password being the immediate case, but this
# now applies to every screen (bookmarking /sales-analysis, or just
# refreshing the browser while on /settings) — is a real HTTP request for
# that literal path, and without this file Netlify would 404 it: there's no
# actual file at build/web/reset-password, only build/web/index.html, which
# is what needs to run for every one of these paths so Flutter's own router
# can then take over client-side.
#
# 200 (not a 301/302) is deliberate — this rewrites the request to serve
# index.html while leaving the browser's address bar showing the original
# URL the user actually asked for, which is what a client-side router needs
# to then read and act on.
/*    /index.html   200
